 # Living Survey: Artificial_General_Intelligence                                                              
                                                                                                               
 ## Introduction                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
 This document collects the scientific literature regarding **Artificial_General_Intelligence**.               
+                                                                                                              
+## Recent Developments and Theoretical Frameworks                                                             
+                                                                                                              
+Recent scholarship continues to explore the architectural, ethical, and policy dimensions of AGI. Theoretical 
work has proposed novel mathematical frameworks for autonomous intelligence, suggesting that consciousness and 
autonomy may emerge from morphogenetic structures and topological integrity rather than traditional            
computational models of the subject [^10.5281_zenodo.19034234]. Concurrently, the pursuit of AGI has sparked   
critical debates regarding its safety and societal implications. Researchers have highlighted the risks of     
framing AGI as an unquestioned goal, arguing that undefined systems like AGI cannot be adequately tested for   
safety and that the drive toward it may perpetuate discriminatory historical paradigms                         
[^10.5210_fm.v29i4.13636].                                                                                     
+                                                                                                              
+In parallel, significant efforts are directed toward ensuring controllable and provably safe AGI systems.     
Formal verification and mechanistic interpretability are proposed as essential pathways to guarantee that      
powerful AGIs satisfy human-specified requirements, thereby mitigating existential risks                       
[^10.48550_arxiv.2309.01933]. The intersection of AGI and robotics also raises profound questions about        
consciousness, with conjectures exploring whether sufficiently advanced general robotic intelligence could     
become indistinguishable from human consciousness or even serve as a substitute in critical roles              
[^10.1109_mpuls.2024.3354609][^10.22339_jbh.v7i4.7403].                                                        
+                                                                                                              
+From a policy and strategic perspective, the conceptualization of AGI remains contested. The European Union's 
recent calls for AGI in healthcare have been critiqued for lacking conceptual discipline, potentially          
conflating advanced narrow AI with qualitatively novel, unpredictable technologies that warrant a precautionary
approach [^10.1016_j.jrt.2026.100183]. Globally, national strategies are actively tracking progress toward     
general AI, with specific focus on machine learning, brain-inspired AI, and brain-computer interfaces as key   
pillars for achieving autonomous capabilities [^10.51593_20210064].                                            
+                                                                                                              
+Methodologically, deep reinforcement learning is increasingly viewed as a general-purpose framework for AGI,  
offering application-independent and platform-independent control architectures that incrementally improve     
intelligence through environmental interaction [^10.48550_arxiv.2105.13806]. Furthermore, the transition from  
narrow AI to more generalized capabilities requires abandoning mere imitation of human problem-solving in favor
of systems that accumulate new knowledge through direct environmental interaction [^10.20948_future-2023-16].  
The broader implications of super-intelligence and human-AI synergy continue to shape psychological and        
philosophical research, emphasizing the need to understand individual cognitive differences in the development 
of future intelligent systems [^10.1016_j.intell.2021.101563].                                                 
                                                                                                               

